Subject: Competitive play: each player sees their own team in its kit
Upstream-base: a353c8f2dfb34eb08fecd725965a46ea629428e3

In a mirror match (tweak patch 0015) one captain is on both teams, and the
away team wears his away kit: on the field and in the menus, the overlays,
the loading screen and the newspaper's photo. On one screen that tells the
teams apart. In a set's mirror match (0052) each player has a screen of their
own, and the players chose to see their own team in its usual kit and the
opponent's in the away kit, whichever side is away. Each game decides this
alone; the match itself is the same on both.

MirrorMatchDressedSide (mscharged_competitive_mirror_dressed_side,
src/platform/competitive_match.cpp) is the side whose team wears the away
kit: the away team's offline and in the draft, whose screens always show this
player's team on side 0; in a set's mirror match, from the match's start (the
host's GameStart sets the sides), the opponent's. The kit's hooks ask for it
instead of side 1:

- MirrorMatchAwayKit, and with it the player markers, the defensive play
  overlay, the goalie's Mega Strike hand and the menus' captain pictures;
- CharacterLoader: the made kits, the Mega Strike hand, the captain's and
  goalie's away kit, and the sidekicks' textures, whose retail branch for one
  captain on both teams dresses team 1 (it stays, the hook overrides its
  names after it);
- the goal banner's emblem, the HUD's captain icon (both icons are checked
  before their images are added), the super ability picture, the menus' team
  colours (SHNavigation, SHChooseSides) and the newspaper photo of a winner in
  the away kit;
- the match loading screen's picture of the dressed team (the home team's
  place, LUIGI, or the away team's, MARIO), now also online, where only a
  set's mirror match has one captain on both teams.

